  "description": "<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd\">\n<html><head><meta name=\"qrichtext\" content=\"1\" /><style type=\"text/css\">\np, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }\n</style></head><body style=\" font-family:'Noto Sans'; font-size:10pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;\">\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><span style=\" font-family:'.SF NS Text'; font-size:13pt;\">LM2576 </span>3A 52KHz 40V Buck DC to DC<span style=\" font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8.25pt;\"> in TO220 package.</span></p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8.25pt;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><span style=\" font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8.25pt;\">Allthough the specifications of the LM2575 (1A) and LM2576 (3A) are far from impressive today, they are still acceptable in many situations. The main advantage of the LM2575/LM2576 is that it is available from many vendors and therefore low-cost and easy to find. Many vendors offer more advanced regulators that are pinout compatible with the LM2576, therefore designing your PCB for the LM2575/LM2576 keeps your options wide open.</span></p>\n<p style=\"-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8.25pt;\"><br /></p>\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\"><span style=\" font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8.25pt;\">Manufacturs of the LM2576 are: Texax Instruments, Microchip, XLSemi (XL2576), HM Semi (HM2576), ON Semi, TAEJin, Huagao Semi.</span></p></body></html>",
